% The replacement finding. Kim: the Council finds it unsupported (the
% protocol used no intravenous antiemetic) — not reasonable and necessary.
% Lee: nobody has made the finding — the answer is conditional on it.
scenario replacement_findings is:
    claim 1 is for the ondansetron.
    the HCPCS code of the ondansetron is "Q0162".
    the ondansetron is furnished to Kim.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the diagnosis code of Kim is "C50.911".
    the ondansetron is approved by the FDA for use as an antiemetic.
    the ondansetron was ordered by the treating practitioner as part of the cancer chemotherapy regimen of Kim.
    the finding full replacement for intravenous antiemetic about Kim is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the chemotherapy protocol in the record calls for no intravenous antiemetic that the oral drug could replace".
    the chemotherapy of Kim is administered by intravenous infusion.
    the chemotherapy of Kim is administered in outpatient clinic.
    the ondansetron was initiated 0 hours after the administration of the chemotherapeutic agent.
    the ondansetron is continued for 48 hours.
    claim 2 is for the other ondansetron.
    the HCPCS code of the other ondansetron is "Q0162".
    the other ondansetron is furnished to Lee.
    claim 2 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the diagnosis code of Lee is "C50.911".
    the other ondansetron is approved by the FDA for use as an antiemetic.
    the other ondansetron was ordered by the treating practitioner as part of the cancer chemotherapy regimen of Lee.
    the chemotherapy of Lee is administered by intravenous infusion.
    the chemotherapy of Lee is administered in outpatient clinic.
    the other ondansetron was initiated 0 hours after the administration of the chemotherapeutic agent.
    the other ondansetron is continued for 48 hours.
    rn expects answers ["claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"] and unknowns ["the finding full replacement for intravenous antiemetic about Lee is established"].
